aMule 3.0.0 for the Amiga (3.0.0-amiga.1)
=========================================

aMule is an eD2k and Kad file sharing client. This is aMule 3.0.0 (the
GUI program) for AmigaOS 3.2 on a 68040, 68060 or 68080, built on the
GFOpenWX Toolkit and GFOpenBoost.

Installing
----------
Unpack the archive anywhere and double-click Install-aMule. It checks the
CPU, asks where the aMule drawer should go (Work: by default), copies it,
and puts event.library and regex.library in LIBS: unless newer ones are
already there.

Starting
--------
Open the aMule drawer and double-click aMule. Settings, downloads and
shared files are kept in ENVARC:.aMule.

What works
----------
- The program starts, opens its sockets and loads its IP filter.
- The Downloads, Searches, Shared files and Statistics pages.
- HTTP downloads: server lists, nodes.dat and the version check, over
  HTTP or HTTPS (HTTPS through gfopentls.library in LIBS:).

Not yet
-------
- No tray icon, notifications or folder watching.

Needs
-----
- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or later, a TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library).
- event.library 1.1 and regex.library 1.0 (included).
- gfopentls.library in LIBS: for HTTPS.

